 <a href=\"/en/surah/18.html\">Surah Al-Kahf</a> › Verse 110</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah Al-Kahf 18:110</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿قُلْ إِنَّمَا أَنَا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ يُوحَىٰ إِلَيَّ أَنَّمَا إِلَٰهُكُمْ إِلَٰهٌ وَاحِدٌ فَمَن كَانَ يَرْجُو لِقَاءَ رَبِّهِ فَلْيَعْمَلْ عَمَلًا صَالِحًا وَلَا يُشْرِكْ بِعِبَادَةِ رَبِّهِ أَحَدًا﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">Say, &quot;I am only a man like you, to whom has been revealed that your god is one God. So whoever would hope for the meeting with his Lord - let him do righteous work and not associate in the worship of his Lord anyone.&quot;</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">&quot; أحدهما &quot; ألا يعبد إلا الله. و &quot; الثاني &quot; أن يعبد بما أمر وشرع لا بغير ذلك من البدع.<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 10/173</cite></blockquote></section><section><h2>Imam Ibn al-Qayyim</h2><h3>What he quoted from others</h3><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><span class=\"who\">أبو علي</span> <span class=\"st\">أقرّه</span> «والخالص: ما كان لله، والصواب: ما كان على السنة،»<cite>«مدارج السالكين بين منازل إياك نعبد وإياك نستعين» 1/105</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s18a110\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/18-109.html\">Previous verse (18:109)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}